orktree CLI where the certificate is current at ed6ba4c4e9b. Implemented as commit 23e07e17e52: 30 files, all within file_impact. Targeted suites 8059 passed; new round-trip integration test passes on Cloud and DC backends (8 cases); lint incl. ratchets and typecheck clean. Not changed: applier._print_batch_recon (advisory, file outside certified scope). make verify running.","timestamp":1794379454427628643},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"2026-11-10 23:15 PST: `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` on 23e07e17e52bf50bd7f959b17e1bdc9ffd20f5f9 (22:44-23:14 PST): exit 0 — default tier 20972 passed / 29 skipped, integration tier 210 passed / 2 skipped. Log .rebar/worktrees/fixver-epic/.rebar/scratch/3d705fec/make-verify-c4.log. make lint (incl. check_complexity_baseline --check and check_mechanism_delta --check) exit 0 on the same commit; largest src/rebar file 799 lines (_ref_lock.py, untouched). Pushed to Gerrit as change 3348.","timestamp":1794381309996701322},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the previous comment: the Gerrit change is 3346 (not 3348).","timestamp":1794381323979350830}],"created_at":1794256428415492001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cbf22e23-2298-4d3d-adc0-816130ac80e7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nJira fix versions now reach rebar, but a rebar release never reaches Jira: no outbound diff compares `releases` and no transport writes fix versions. This child implements rebar→Jira per ADR 0124 (decisions 5, 6), following tags→labels, for both adapters.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Transport.** Add `add_fix_version(remote_id, name)`/`remove_fix_version(remote_id, name)` to the `TicketTransport` protocol in `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py` (beside `add_label`/`remove_label`) and to `_REQUIRED_TRANSPORT_MEMBERS` (conformance guard). Per-item verbs only, never `set`:\n   - Cloud (`adapters/jira/acli_graph.py`, beside `add_label`): `self._direct_rest_put_raw(f\"/rest/api/3/issue/{key}\", {\"update\": {\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]}})`; remove uses `{\"remove\": {\"name\": name}}`. Non-2xx raises `HTTPError`.\n   - DC (`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, beside `remove_label`): `issue.update(update={\"fixVersions\": [{\"add\": {\"name\": name}}]})`, through `_call_logged` as `remove_label` does.\n   - Test transports with `remove_label` gain both verbs (`tests/unit/reconciler/`: `backend_support.py`, `apply/_sync_only_dispatch_probe.py`, `mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py`, `mutate/test_outbound_update_combined.py`, `orchestrate/test_e2e_dedup_pass.py`, `orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py`; and `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py`); `test_transport_port_completeness.py`'s `_REQUIRED` lists them. Write inventories gain both: `_CLASSIFIED_MUTATING`, `_POOLED_REST_MEMBERS` and `_DC_SWEPT` in `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py`, the `mutations` dict in `test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py`, and `MUTATING_TRANSPORT_METHODS` in `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/_cloud_s3_support.py`.\n2. **Intent.** In `local_label_intent.py` move `compute_label_intent_set`'s directory walk into `_ever_seen(ticket_id, tracker_dir, extractor)` (tags behavior unchanged) and add `compute_release_intent_map(bound_local_ids, tracker_dir)` using it: names from non-inbound `RELEASE_DELTA.added` and `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state.releases` (ADR 0124 decision 5); `source == \"inbound\"` deltas are skipped and `.removed` is never folded, as for tags. Shared label limit: a compaction SNAPSHOT folds inbound-origin names into intent. `outbound_pass.py` computes it beside `compute_label_intent_map` and passes `local_release_intent` on `OutboundDiffConfig`.\n3. **Diff.** New `outbound_releases.py`: `_diff_releases(ticket, jira_fields, intent_set)` mirrors `outbound_labels._diff_labels`; names come from the existing `_jira_release_names` (delivered by the inbound child, `inbound_collection_diffs.py:217`, reused unchanged); a non-list `fixVersions` yields `[]`; ADD a local name missing in Jira and REMOVE a Jira name missing locally, each only when the name is in `intent_set` (bug a06c). Records are `{\"action\", \"release\"}`.\n4. **Mutation and payload.** Add `releases` to `OutboundMutation`, call `_diff_releases` in the bound-update builder (`outbound_mutation_builders._compute_outbound_update_mutation`), and include it in the emit condition and `RECON: outbound_update` log. In `mutation_payloads.OutboundUpdatePayload` add `releases` to the fields, `_OUTBOUND_UPDATE_KEYS`, the non-empty check, `as_legacy_dict` (only when non-empty, keeping manifests and the canonical hash unchanged) and `from_legacy`. `outbound_pass.py` passes `releases=tuple(getattr(om, \"releases\", []))`; `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict` reads `getattr(typed, \"releases\", ())` (create payloads have none) / `payload.get(\"releases\", [])` and emits `\"releases\"`.\n5. **Dispatch.** `dispatch_one._update_one_dispatch_releases(mutation, client, issue_key)` mirrors `_update_one_dispatch_labels`: per item; a failure is logged to stderr (an `HTTPError` with up to 500 bytes of Jira's error body) and retried next pass; counts go to `subop_applied` as `releases_computed`/`releases_applied`. `apply_handlers.py` exposes `releases_applied` and adds `\"releases\"` to the silent-no-op canary kinds.\n6. **Suppression.** Already wired by the inbound child.\n7. **Create path.** A new Jira issue gets its releases on the next bound-update pass; the create payload is unchanged.\n8. **Docs.** In `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` mark the fix-versions outbound cell supported (per-item add/remove), with a \"pending live verification (ADR 0124; checked by plucky-jetblack-parrot)\" note: the version must already exist in the Jira project, and Fix versions may need to be on the project's edit screen.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/`: `_backend.py`, `adapters/jira/acli_graph.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, `local_label_intent.py`, `outbound_releases.py` (new), `outbound_differ.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_pass.py`, `mutation_payloads.py`, `batch_dispatch.py`, `dispatch_one.py`, `apply_handlers.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- New tests: `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py`, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py`\n- Extended tests: `mutate/test_local_label_intent.py`, `test_field_contract_properties.py`, `mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py`, `test_transport_port_completeness.py`, `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py`, `test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py`, `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/_cloud_s3_support.py`, and the 7 test transports in step 1\n\n## Testing\n\n- Transport: Cloud add sends `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/REB-1` with the step 1 body (captured `urllib` request), remove the `remove` body; a 400 raises `HTTPError`. DC calls `issue.update(update=...)` with the same item. Neither sends `set` or `fields.fixVersions`.\n- Diff: local `[\"2.4\"]`, Jira `[]`, 2.4 in intent → add; not in intent → `[]`; local `[]`, Jira `[\"2.4\"]`, in intent → remove; not in intent → `[]`; unobserved → `[]`.\n- Intent: an inbound `RELEASE_DELTA` adds nothing; a local delta's added names and SNAPSHOT releases are included; removed names are not.\n- Payload: `OutboundUpdatePayload` round-trips with and without releases, and a releases-free payload projects no `releases` key; a releases-only payload is valid; `_mutation_to_batch_dict` carries releases and gives a create payload `[]`.\n- Dispatch: a failing write logs Jira's error body and the next item still runs; computed > 0, applied 0 trips the canary.\n- Suppression: a real `OutboundMutation` adding 2.4 drops the inbound REMOVE of 2.4.\n- Round trip (integration, Cloud- and DC-shaped fakes): a local add pushes one add, then a no-op pass writes nothing; removing it locally pushes one remove; a Jira-side add arrives as one `RELEASE_DELTA`; a Jira-side removal of an inbound-origin name gives one inbound remove and zero Jira writes; a new issue gets its release on the pass after create.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A local release add produces exactly one per-item `fixVersions` add on the next pass, on Cloud and DC; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Removing a locally added release produces exactly one per-item `fixVersions` remove; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Cloud and DC request bodies match step 1; pinned by the transport test.\n- [ ] A Jira fix version rebar never held is never removed; pinned by the diff test.\n- [ ] A Jira-side removal of an inbound-origin release on an uncompacted ticket is not undone; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] A no-change pass writes nothing to Jira or rebar; pinned by the round-trip test.\n- [ ] Release records reach `update_one` through `outbound_pass` and `batch_dispatch`; pinned by the payload test.\n- [ ] Existing outbound manifest shapes are unchanged; pinned by the existing manifest tests.\n- [ ] Existing label outbound and dispatch tests pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] No `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py","reason":"transport verbs + required members"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py","reason":"Cloud fix-version write"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","reason":"DC fix-version write"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/local_label_intent.py","reason":"release intent map"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py","reason":"new outbound diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"mutation field and config"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py","reason":"call release diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py","reason":"intent + payload releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py","reason":"outbound payload releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"batch dict releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"release dispatch"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"releases_applied + canary"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"outbound cell + prerequisites"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_local_label_intent.py","reason":"release intent"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py","reason":"intent gate"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py","reason":"outbound releases round-trip"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness.py","reason":"required verbs"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep.py","reason":"classify new Cloud writes"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_rate_limit_retry.py","reason":"DC mutations inventory"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/_cloud_s3_support.py","reason":"read-only guard inventory"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/backend_support.py","reason":"FakeTransport verbs"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/apply/_sync_only_dispatch_probe.py","reason":"transport verbs"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","reason":"transport verbs"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconcil